{
  "id": "volume_in_horizontal_pipes_or_cylindrical_tanks",
  "title": "Volume in Horizontal Pipes or Cylindrical Tanks",
  "description": "Calculate liquid content in partly filled horizontal pipes or tanks. Provides volume based on liquid level height and tank diameter.",
  "type": "calculator",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Volume in Horizontal Pipes or Cylindrical Tanks\n\nThis calculator determines the liquid volume in partly filled horizontal pipes or cylindrical tanks based on:\n- **Liquid Level (m)**: The height of liquid in the tank\n- **Diameter (m)**: The diameter of the horizontal pipe or tank\n\nThe calculation uses standard geometric formulas for a cylindrical tank viewed from the side, where the liquid forms a circular segment."
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "liquid_level",
          "label": "Liquid Level",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "m",
          "defaultValue": 0.5
        },
        {
          "id": "diameter",
          "label": "Diameter of Tank or Pipe",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "m",
          "defaultValue": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "length",
          "label": "Length of Tank or Pipe",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "m",
          "defaultValue": 1
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "volume",
          "label": "Volume",
          "unit": "m³",
          "formula": "inputs.length * (Math.pow(inputs.diameter/2, 2) * Math.acos((inputs.diameter/2 - inputs.liquid_level) / (inputs.diameter/2)) - (inputs.diameter/2 - inputs.liquid_level) * Math.sqrt(inputs.liquid_level * inputs.diameter - Math.pow(inputs.liquid_level, 2)))",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
